{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git diff --check -- game/games/lanterns && git diff -- game/games/lanterns/logic/src/lib.rs game/games/lanterns/app.contract game/games/lanterns/assets/lanterns-adapter.mjs game/games/lanterns/README.md'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/game/games/lanterns/README.md b/game/games/lanterns/README.md\nindex 98f1be5..18c42de 100644\n--- a/game/games/lanterns/README.md\n+++ b/game/games/lanterns/README.md\n@@ -3,7 +3,8 @@\n A three-minute third-person game built on Exact's game add-on. Move the animated\n Fox with WASD, arrows, or the left side of a touch screen. Jump with Space or the\n purple button and press E or LIGHT within 1.5 metres of a lantern. Push the crate\n-to reach the twelfth lantern on the ledge.\n+to reach the twelfth lantern on the ledge, then return within two metres of the\n+starting clearing before dusk ends.\n \n From the repository root:\n \ndiff --git a/game/games/lanterns/app.contract b/game/games/lanterns/app.contract\nindex 8f0bde0..20e41fd 100644\n--- a/game/games/lanterns/app.contract\n+++ b/game/games/lanterns/app.contract\n@@ -69,6 +69,8 @@ component Lanterns\n               text checkpointStatus aria-live=\"polite\" testId=\"save-status\" padding=10 border-radius=9 background-color=\"#1b1730\" color=\"#ffd27a\" font-size=14\n           text \"Move: WASD / arrows / left thumb\" position=\"absolute\" bottom=22 left=22 padding=12 border-radius=10 background-color=\"#1b1730\" color=\"#d6cdec\" font-size=15\n           text \"Push the crate beside the high ledge. Jump onto it, then jump again.\" testId=\"sign-instruction\" position=\"absolute\" bottom=76 left=22 right=22 padding=12 border-radius=10 background-color=\"#1b1730\" color=\"#ffd27a\" font-size=14\n+          when hud.phase == \"returning\"\n+            text \"All twelve are lit — return home to the starting clearing!\" aria-live=\"assertive\" testId=\"return-home-instruction\" position=\"absolute\" top=94 left=\"24%\" width=\"52%\" padding=16 text-align=\"center\" border-radius=10 background-color=\"#ffd27a\" color=\"#241531\" font-size=19 font-weight=700\n           row position=\"absolute\" bottom=22 right=22 gap=14 align-items=\"flex-end\"\n             button press=light testId=\"light\" width=92 height=92 display=\"flex\" border-radius=46 background-color=\"#ffb43b\" justify-content=\"center\" align-items=\"center\"\n               text \"LIGHT\" width=\"100%\" text-align=\"center\" color=\"#241531\" font-size=17 font-weight=700\n@@ -83,7 +85,7 @@ component Lanterns\n           when hud.phase == \"won\"\n             column testId=\"victory\" position=\"absolute\" top=\"28%\" left=\"24%\" width=\"52%\" padding=30 align-items=\"center\" gap=18 border-radius=14 background-color=\"#1b1730\"\n               text \"The island is glowing\" aria-live=\"polite\" font-size=34 color=\"#ffd27a\" font-weight=700\n-              text \"All twelve lanterns are lit.\" font-size=18 color=\"#fff4d6\"\n+              text \"All twelve lanterns are lit, and the fox made it home.\" font-size=18 color=\"#fff4d6\"\n               button press=restart testId=\"again\" padding=16 border-radius=9 background-color=\"#ffd27a\"\n                 text \"Play again\" font-size=19 color=\"#241531\"\n           when hud.phase == \"lost\"\n@@ -95,7 +97,7 @@ component Lanterns\n         else\n           column testId=\"title\" position=\"absolute\" top=0 left=0 width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" align-items=\"center\" justify-content=\"center\" gap=24 background-color=\"#130f24\"\n             text \"LANTERNS\" font-size=64 font-weight=700 color=\"#ffd27a\"\n-            text \"Light twelve lanterns before the last three minutes of dusk run out.\" font-size=20 color=\"#fff4d6\"\n+            text \"Light twelve lanterns, then return home before the last three minutes of dusk run out.\" font-size=20 color=\"#fff4d6\"\n             text \"Push the crate to reach the lantern on the stone ledge.\" font-size=17 color=\"#d6cdec\"\n             text \"WASD or arrows · Space to jump · E to light\" font-size=15 color=\"#a99fc1\"\n             row gap=12\ndiff --git a/game/games/lanterns/assets/lanterns-adapter.mjs b/game/games/lanterns/assets/lanterns-adapter.mjs\nindex 6b6ed63..733c43e 100644\n--- a/game/games/lanterns/assets/lanterns-adapter.mjs\n+++ b/game/games/lanterns/assets/lanterns-adapter.mjs\n@@ -86,7 +86,8 @@ if (ENABLED) {\n       if (/\\bjump$/.test(line)) return [{type: 'jump'}];\n       const lit = /\\b(lantern-\\d+) lit$/.exec(line);\n       if (lit) return [{type: 'lantern-lit', id: lit[1]}];\n-      if (/\\ball lanterns lit$/.test(line)) return [{type: 'win'}];\n+      if (/\\ball lanterns lit$/.test(line)) return [{type: 'return-home'}];\n+      if (/\\breturned home$/.test(line)) return [{type: 'win'}];\n       if (/\\bnight fell$/.test(line)) return [{type: 'lose'}];\n       return [];\n     });\ndiff --git a/game/games/lanterns/logic/src/lib.rs b/game/games/lanterns/logic/src/lib.rs\nindex fa98adf..7c487b2 100644\n--- a/game/games/lanterns/logic/src/lib.rs\n+++ b/game/games/lanterns/logic/src/lib.rs\n@@ -57,6 +57,12 @@ struct Actors {\n const FOX_BYTES: &[u8] = include_bytes!(\"../../assets/Fox.glb\");\n const DURATION_TICKS: u32 = 180 * 60;\n const SPAWN: Vec3 = Vec3::new(0.0, 0.0, 12.0);\n+const HOME_RADIUS: f32 = 2.0;\n+const PHASE_TITLE: u32 = 0;\n+const PHASE_PLAYING: u32 = 1;\n+const PHASE_RETURNING: u32 = 2;\n+const PHASE_WON: u32 = 3;\n+const PHASE_LOST: u32 = 4;\n /// Canvas inputs. Action counters let Contract overlay buttons feed distinct\n /// touch presses while the left thumb remains on the raw movement stick.\n #[derive(Default, exact_game::Args)]\n@@ -106,7 +112,7 @@ pub struct Lantern {\n pub struct Session {\n     /// Active fixed ticks; pause and terminal states do not add to this.\n     pub elapsed: u32,\n-    /// 0 title, 1 playing, 2 won, 3 lost.\n+    /// 0 title, 1 playing, 2 returning home, 3 won, 4 lost.\n     pub phase: u32,\n     /// Last Contract Jump counter consumed.\n     pub jump_press: u32,\n@@ -235,14 +241,18 @@ impl Game for Lanterns {\n     fn tick(world: &mut World, input: &Input, args: &Options) {\n         let ids = world.resource::<Session>().actors;\n         let (terminal, jump_button, light_button) = world.edit_resource::<Session, _>(|session| {\n-            if session.phase == 0 && args.started {\n-                session.phase = 1;\n+            if session.phase == PHASE_TITLE && args.started {\n+                session.phase = PHASE_PLAYING;\n             }\n             let jump = session.jump_press != args.jump_press;\n             let light = session.light_press != args.light_press;\n             session.jump_press = args.jump_press;\n             session.light_press = args.light_press;\n-            (session.phase >= 2, jump, light)\n+            (\n+                matches!(session.phase, PHASE_WON | PHASE_LOST),\n+                jump,\n+                light,\n+            )\n         });\n         if terminal {\n             publish(world);\n@@ -285,11 +295,14 @@ impl Game for Lanterns {\n         update_lanterns(world);\n         let elapsed = world.resource::<Session>().elapsed;\n         if elapsed >= DURATION_TICKS {\n-            world.resource_mut::<Session>().phase = 3;\n+            world.resource_mut::<Session>().phase = PHASE_LOST;\n             world.log(\"night fell\");\n             if args.sound {\n                 world.play(\"night\").start();\n             }\n+        } else if let Err(error) = finish_if_home(world, args.sound) {\n+            world.log(error);\n+            return;\n         }\n         update_sun(world, ids.sun);\n         scene::follow(world);\n@@ -490,12 +503,30 @@ fn light_nearest(world: &mut World, sound: bool) -> Result<(), exact_game::KindE\n         world.play(\"chime\").at(entity.entity()).start();\n     }\n     if world.rows::<Lamp>().all(|row| row.lantern.lit) {\n-        world.resource_mut::<Session>().phase = 2;\n+        world.resource_mut::<Session>().phase = PHASE_RETURNING;\n         world.log(\"all lanterns lit\");\n     }\n     Ok(())\n }\n \n+fn finish_if_home(world: &mut World, sound: bool) -> Result<(), exact_game::KindError> {\n+    if world.resource::<Session>().phase != PHASE_RETURNING {\n+        return Ok(());\n+    }\n+    let hero = world.resource::<Session>().actors.hero;\n+    let position = world.row(hero)?.transform.position;\n+    let from_home = Vec2::new(position.x - SPAWN.x, position.z - SPAWN.z);\n+    if from_home.length_squared() > HOME_RADIUS * HOME_RADIUS {\n+        return Ok(());\n+    }\n+    world.resource_mut::<Session>().phase = PHASE_WON;\n+    world.log(\"returned home\");\n+    if sound {\n+        world.play(\"chime\").at(hero.entity()).start();\n+    }\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+\n fn update_lanterns(world: &mut World) {\n     let now = world.now();\n     for row in world.rows::<Lamp>() {\n@@ -524,9 +555,10 @@ fn publish(world: &mut World) {\n         .saturating_sub(world.resource::<Session>().elapsed)\n         .div_ceil(60);\n     let phase = match world.resource::<Session>().phase {\n-        0 => \"title\",\n-        1 => \"playing\",\n-        2 => \"won\",\n+        PHASE_TITLE => \"title\",\n+        PHASE_PLAYING => \"playing\",\n+        PHASE_RETURNING => \"returning\",\n+        PHASE_WON => \"won\",\n         _ => \"lost\",\n     };\n     world.publish(\"count\", count);\n@@ -603,7 +635,7 @@ mod tests {\n     fn no_input_loses_at_exactly_three_minutes() {\n         let mut sim = game();\n         sim.run(180_000.0);\n-        assert_eq!(sim.world().resource::<Session>().phase, 3);\n+        assert_eq!(sim.world().resource::<Session>().phase, PHASE_LOST);\n         assert_eq!(sim.world().resource::<Session>().elapsed, DURATION_TICKS);\n     }\n }\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The core change is in place: lighting all twelve now enters a saved, nonterminal `returning` phase; elapsed time and physics continue; only horizontal proximity within 2 units of the original spawn produces victory, and the 180-second cutoff is checked first. The UI now presents a dedicated, assertive return-home banner during that phase. I’m compiling and running the full Lanterns logic suite now before extending the ordinary-input route proof."}}
